# Equinox lets Cleansing resolve when the players could pay for every land of Bot1's (the owner's rule for Cleansing,
# 2026-11-27): Bot1 controls nine lands and Bot2 eight, Bot1 has 4 life and Bot2 5. The 9 life they could pay between
# them is exactly enough to spare all nine of Bot1's lands - no more lands than life - so the destruction depends on what
# they choose, and Cleansing is not countered (rulings: not if it destroys a land only if a choice is made). Bot2's eight
# lands are not Bot1's and count for nothing. Then no one pays, and all seventeen are destroyed.

